Layout
  foundation.css  upstream app/globals.css "GENERIC FOUNDATION": tokens (:root, .dark), @theme, base rules,
                  primitive-* spacing utilities and shared keyframes. Smooth shadow stacks come from
                  shadow-plugin (Florian Kiem, MIT). Fonts are self-hosted latin subsets instead of next/font;
                  the gallery's striped page, showcase gestures and docs-nav scroller are omitted; reduced-motion,
                  forced-colors and CJK tracking floors are appended. Accessibility: ink-3 is lifted to the 3:1
                  non-text floor on every ground (light 0.695→0.619, dark 0.541→0.582 OKLCH lightness), and small
                  informational text uses ink-2 (≥ 4.5:1); `color-scheme` follows the `.dark` theme.
  atoms/          upstream components/atoms, with the `cn` import path and "use client" adjusted.
                  Switch and SegmentedControl use non-submit buttons so form settings change without submitting;
                  further component-specific accessibility adaptations are documented inline.
  primitives/     upstream components/primitives. Each primitive keeps upstream markup, class names, tokens,
                  radii and motion. Allowed adaptations: demo data and scripted timers replaced by props and
                  callbacks carrying real state; i18n strings and accessibility; commercial Central Icons replaced
                  by open icons; remote images, sounds and marketing removed. A primitive's COMPONENT-SPECIFIC CSS
                  block from upstream globals.css sits next to it. TaskRows scopes detail IDs to each instance
                  so repeated task keys in separate lists retain correct accessibility associations.
  controls/       platform controls upstream does not ship (inputs, select, dialog, sheet, notice, empty state),
                  composed only from upstream tokens and primitives.

npm packages used by upstream primitives: liveline (InsightCards charts, MIT), glimm (PromptBar accent sweep,
MIT), shadow-plugin (MIT).

Fonts: Inter and JetBrains Mono latin subsets are self-hosted from @fontsource-variable packages
(SIL Open Font License 1.1: public/licenses/inter-OFL.txt, public/licenses/jetbrains-mono-OFL.txt);
no third-party font request is made.
